{
  "description": "<div data-editor-id=\"84f0878c-7447-4f25-92ff-89e415571260\"><p><span style=\"font-size: 1.5rem\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); text-decoration: inherit\" data-color-scope=\"outer\"><span>This video examines who should be accountable for designing, running, and acting on engagement processes. It introduces three criteria for picking the right owner — trust, reach, and authority to act — and explains how AI can expand who is able to lead engagement.</span></span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2rem\"><span style=\"color: rgb(222, 222, 222); text-decoration: inherit\" data-color-scope=\"inner\">Last Updated: July 24, 2026</span></span></p></div>",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "description": "",
      "id": "ULEdY6rbm83dE-dEnWdKXn2g0rqikl2b",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "nIitQ5RbkULwfYbCstA46SpjgBXr8Pdf",
          "settings": {
            "paddingTop": 3,
            "quotesInline": false,
            "audioPosition": "bottom",
            "paddingBottom": 3,
